[h1]Caching, Errors & Common Patterns[/h1]

[h2]Caching[/h2]

Tooltip callbacks run [b]every frame[/b] while hovering. If your callback does anything more than reading a couple fields, cache it:

[code]
cacheable = true,
[/code]

The framework records your ctx method calls once, then replays them from a display list. Your code literally doesn't run on subsequent frames.

Cache auto-refreshes every 60 frames (~1 second). Tune it:
[code]
cacheable = true, maxAge = 30,   -- refresh every ~0.5s
cacheable = true, maxAge = 0,    -- never auto-refresh
[/code]

[b]Gotcha:[/b] cache keys on the item ID + detail state. If your output depends on external state (player perks, time of day), provide a cacheKey:

[code]
cacheable = true,
cacheKey = function(item)
    return tostring(item:getModData().myVersion or 0)
end,
[/code]

Or invalidate manually when your state changes:
[code]
TooltipLib.invalidateCache("MyMod_Feature")
[/code]

[b]Caching only works for item and itemSlot surfaces.[/b] Object, skill, vehicle, and recipe surfaces don't support it.

[h2]Error Handling — Circuit Breaker[/h2]

Every callback is pcall-wrapped. If yours throws, other providers keep running. But if you have a persistent bug, the [b]circuit breaker[/b] kicks in: 10 consecutive errors and your provider is auto-disabled for the session.

You'll see in the log:
[code]
[TooltipLib] Provider 'MyMod' disabled after 10 consecutive errors.
Call TooltipLib.resetProvider('MyMod') to re-enable.
[/code]

A single successful render resets the counter. Only persistent every-frame errors trip it.

[h2]Common Patterns[/h2]

[h3]Optional dependency on TooltipLib[/h3]

If TooltipLib is nice-to-have but not required:
[code]
if TooltipLib and TooltipLib.checkVersion("1.0.0") then
    TooltipLib.registerProvider({ ... })
end
[/code]

If it's a hard dependency, use minVersion in registration:
[code]
minVersion = "1.0.0",  -- rejects with a clear log if too old
[/code]

[h3]Item providers auto-apply to crafting slots[/h3]

Your target="item" provider will also appear in ISToolTipItemSlot (crafting panel) automatically. If you need to hide content in crafting context:
[code]
callback = function(ctx)
    if ctx.surface == "itemSlot" then return end
    -- item-only content here
end,
[/code]

[h3]World object provider (generators example)[/h3]

[code]
TooltipLib.registerProvider({
    id = "MyMod_Generator",
    target = "object",
    enabled = TooltipLib.Filters.generator,
    description = "Generator status",
    callback = function(ctx)
        local gen = ctx.object
        if gen:isActivated() then
            ctx:addLabel("Running", TooltipLib.Colors.GREEN)
        else
            ctx:addLabel("Off", TooltipLib.Colors.RED)
        end
        ctx:addProgress("Fuel:", gen:getFuel() / 100)
    end,
})
[/code]

[h3]Skill provider[/h3]

[code]
TooltipLib.registerProvider({
    id = "MyMod_SkillXP",
    target = "skill",
    description = "XP multiplier",
    enabled = function(perk, level)
        return level < 10
    end,
    callback = function(ctx)
        local ok, mult = pcall(function()
            return ctx.player:getXp():getMultiplier(ctx.perk)
        end)
        if ok and mult then
            ctx:addFloat("XP Mult:", mult, 2, true)
        end
    end,
})
[/code]

[h3]Custom colors[/h3]

Built-in colors are frozen (read-only). Define your own as {r, g, b, a}:
[code]
local MY_TEAL = {0.2, 0.8, 0.7, 1.0}
ctx:addLabel("Enchanted", MY_TEAL)
[/code]

[h2]Debugging[/h2]

[code]
TooltipLib.debug = true  -- verbose logging (cache, filters, etc.)

-- What's registered?
local providers = TooltipLib.getProviders()
for _, p in ipairs(providers) do
    print(p.id, p.target, p.priority)
end

-- Quick checks
TooltipLib.hasProvider("MyMod")
TooltipLib.getProviderCount("item")
[/code]

[h2]Full API[/h2]

[code]
TooltipLib.registerProvider(options)              -- register
TooltipLib.removeProvider("id")                  -- unregister
TooltipLib.replaceProvider(options)               -- atomic remove+register
TooltipLib.resetProvider("id")                   -- re-enable after breaker
TooltipLib.setProviderEnabled("id", bool)        -- player toggle
TooltipLib.isProviderEnabled("id")               -- check toggle
TooltipLib.invalidateCache("id")                 -- clear one cache
TooltipLib.invalidateCache()                     -- clear all
TooltipLib.invalidateActiveProviders()           -- re-eval all filters
TooltipLib.hasProvider("id")                     -- exists?
TooltipLib.getProviderCount()                    -- total count
TooltipLib.getProviders()                        -- introspection
TooltipLib.getHookStatus()                       -- hook install status
TooltipLib.checkVersion("1.0.0")                 -- version check
TooltipLib.VERSION                               -- "1.1.0"
[/code]
